# Answer

An answer page addresses one narrow question without splitting it into a multi-step journey. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/answer/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use this format for a small household or documentation question, such as the difference between a palette and a display mode. Put the answer first, followed by essential context and a link to the relevant setting or detailed guide. It should be possible to understand the main answer from the opening paragraph.

## Structure and behaviour

Use one descriptive page title, a concise answer, optional supporting headings and a small related-navigation group. Keep live values out of permanent prose unless the page reads and labels the current state. A document about a setting should not appear to confirm that the user has changed it.

## Home Assistant boundary

This is a reference content template. It does not create a new HA panel or substitute a static answer for a device’s current state. Avoid government service metadata and do not add a promotional or feedback form without a real purpose and endpoint.

