## Acceptance checks

- The first paragraph answers the title.
- Necessary qualifications appear beside the answer.
- Links use real destination labels.
- A simple answer is not artificially divided into tabs.

Check the examples at narrow widths, with a keyboard and without JavaScript. Test a production implementation against its actual data and permissions before calling it supported.

## Sources and maintenance

Reviewed against the official guidance on 11 November 2026. The [source and migration record](../source-history.html) separates the Publishing Design Guide from the component gem and records the metadata-history migration. Use civica.uk branding and the local font and colour tokens; official GOV.UK marks, analytics and account services are not part of this adaptation.

